[TITLE]
;;Project Title/Notes
Pumps under dynamic wave, ramped, constant and pulsed inflows, SI units - noodl test fixture
One subsystem per pump kind: inflow junction Jk -> conduit Ck -> wet well Wk (a junction whose
surface area is the 100 m2 MIN_SURFAREA floor) -> pump Pk -> fixed outfall Ok. A, H: PUMP3 with startup and
shutoff depths (H against a lift of 2.5 m); B: PUMP2 steps in the well depth; C: PUMP4,
continuous in it; D: PUMP1 steps in the volume of a storage well (50 m2); F: an ideal pump.
The pulses and curves are chosen so that SWMM converges on every step (a stepped pump curve
crossed by a rising or falling well can have no fixed point inside a step).

